  "rationale": "The prompt asks which channel has a message reacted to with thumbsup by an admin/owner. The base seed contains exactly one reaction record (message 1706110000.000100, user U01AGENBOT9, reaction_type 'eyes') and no thumbsup reactions anywhere, so 'absent' is the correct resolution: no conversation satisfies the full route (CONVERSATION→MESSAGE→REACTION→USER→WORKSPACE_MEMBERSHIP). All role facts are verified against base_seed: the eyes-reaction message and its author Lukas in #engineering (C03IJKL9012), the explicit message_reactions row for the eyes emoji, the reactor's plain 'member' role in user_teams, and two genuine admins (Robert Walsh, Morgan Freeman) who hold admin role but have zero reaction activity, correctly showing the role condition is meaningful yet unmet. Entity names now correctly map to actual schema tables (channels, messages, message_reactions, users, user_teams), and the obligation's table 'channels' aligns with the referent_entity CONVERSATION per the domain model's Conversation↔Channel mapping, resolving the earlier mechanical flag (now empty). The binding_note correctly requires same-user linkage between reaction and admin/owner membership. Negatives are well-differentiated (wrong emoji, wrong role, no reaction) and derived from real seed content without hinting the answer. The access_plan (list→history→reactions.get→users.info) is realistic and uses only documented API capabilities. No validity or quality defects found."
